# Release-critical markdown: prettier rewrites `[comment]: <> (START OF GITHUB README)` into
# `[comment]: <> 'START OF GITHUB README'`. The Makefile slices the published README between those
# markers, so they are left exactly as-is. .prettierrc also sets useTabs, so prettier re-tabs the
# fenced code blocks that markdownlint's MD010 then de-tabs, and .husky/pre-commit runs prettier -w
# before pre-commit -- the two fight on every commit that touches README.md. Both files are also
# copies of src/README.md and src/RELEASE.md (src/package.json "postbuild") and src/ is ignored
# below, so formatting them here only creates drift the next build overwrites. Markdown style is
# owned by markdownlint-cli2.
README.md
RELEASE.md
# Markdown style is owned by markdownlint-cli2, not prettier (same reason as README.md/RELEASE.md).
CLAUDE.md
# Owned by their own tools; prettier's -w reflow of the giticket `args:` array leaves
# .pre-commit-config.yaml unstaged, which makes the chained `pre-commit run` in .husky/pre-commit
# abort with "Your pre-commit configuration is unstaged".
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.markdownlint-cli2.yaml
